  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next`. The last step of its Workflow checklist, step 7, starts with \"Next:\" and names the bundled skill `habeas-requirements`. That is where findings that need code, tests, or requirement text changes go next. `habeas-requirements` exists as `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. Step 5 covers the other outcomes, such as a finding that needs the user or a gap to defer. Those lead to no further task, so the requirement lets the workflow name no skill for them. Step 6, committing the evidence, is the only other step after it. `habeas-refactor` is named in the front matter description as the skill to use before this one, so it is not a next-task obligation. No violation-query match was listed for this site.",
